   "adjustments": [],
   "text": "Gets delayed cortisol spikes at the wrong hour and the brain never gets a clean sleep window. The result is fragmented rest, slower reaction times and a higher risk of errors, that weekly jet lag is why night work shreds sleep quality. So the body clock isn't just a suggestion. It's a hard -wired timer that expects bright light in the morning and darkness at night. And when we flip that schedule the timer keeps ticking on its original rhythm. When that timer gets scrambled night after night, the whole system pays the price, hormones, metabolism, even mood, and that's what we'll tackle next. You might notice that after a string of nights you feel groggy even on days off."
  },
  {
   "id": "clip_ee088422",
   "rank": 2,
   "start": 329.38,
   "end": 367.81,
   "duration": 38.43,
   "title": "The biggest mistake I see is staying awake",
